// computation kernel
// imgIn, imgOut, y1, y2: i x j
//
// The filter is separable and implemented as 4 1D recursive passes:
//   1) causal along j
//   2) anti-causal along j
//      -> combined into vertical result in imgOut
//   3) causal along i
//   4) anti-causal along i
//      -> final combine into imgOut
//
// Each 1D pass has dependencies along its scan direction,
// but different rows/columns are independent and can be parallelized.
[[gnu::flatten, gnu::noinline]]
void kernel_deriche(num_t alpha, auto imgIn, auto imgOut, auto y1, auto y2) {
